# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Get Medieval (KCD), 61 min of real streamed gameplay on the release policy, b:vsync -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -etw -dejit 2026-09-22, first build on our own NvFBC declarations; menus and desktop trimmed off both ends
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Get Medieval (KCD), 61 min of real streamed gameplay on the release policy, b:vsync -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -etw -dejit 2026-09-22, first build on our own NvFBC declarations; menus and desktop trimmed off both ends
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 61
field_long_runs 10
field_synth_pct 1.0
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the residual blend-zone class at the highest rate yet seen, 10 runs >= 50 in
# an hour against 0917_1's 8 in 90 minutes. Every one follows a lock release at a small source
# hitch (a 29 to 31 ms gap in the game's flips about 3 s before) and a slow re-engage. The lock
# released 44 times an hour here against 16 on the 2026-09-16 stream, at the same rate of small
# hitches (118 against 129 an hour): 29 of 120 hitches dropped the lock here, 5 of 88 there.
# The real lock driven by this capture's own error sequence reproduces the field lock state on
# 99.8% of presents, so the releases follow from this timeline. Why it releases so much more
# often is unexplained.
#
# WINDOW. The log starts at the desktop, the game launches at 5 s and loads into gameplay at
# about 279 s, and the stream stopped at 4351 s. Cut 400 s to 4050 s, a margin of about 5
# minutes inside the stream at each end, so no menu or desktop time is inside. No second in the
# window exceeds 130 arrivals.
#
# FIDELITY. Replay and field agree on synth (1.1% against 1.0%) and worst run (62 against 61).
# Runs >= 50 read 7 against 10 because the field population sits on the threshold: two runs of
# 49 and four of exactly 50, so a replayed run one present shorter drops out of the count. The
# dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, reads 9 against 10, worst 62 against 61.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the release policy.
max_worst_run 62
max_long_runs 7
max_synth_pct 1.5
min_reseeds 32
src_hint 60.0
arrivals 424396
